    "result": "Perfect! The bug is fixed. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## The Problem\nThe `frai gate init --ci` command was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file because the `--ci` flag was not being passed through to the frai-gate CLI. The frai-cli was using Commander to parse the arguments, but only forwarding the positional arguments to the spawned frai-gate process, while the flags were being dropped.\n\n## The Solution\nI modified the `gate` command in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 753-754) to capture all raw arguments from `process.argv`, not just the positional ones. Now when the gate subcommand is invoked, all arguments including flags are properly passed to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n**Key changes:**\n- Line 753-754: Extract all arguments from `process.argv` starting after the 'gate' position\n- Line 755: Pass these complete arguments to the spawned process\n\n## Verification\nAfter rebuilding with `pnpm --filter frai build`, testing `node <repo>/packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js gate init --ci` now correctly creates:\n1. \u2705 `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n2. \u2705 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n\nThe workflow file contains the proper CI configuration that runs `frai-gate check` on every PR.",
